ets scalar-replace see a map-literal arg through the call boundary);\n  a non-trivial arg maps the param to a fresh :local that a wrapping let binds.\n\n  cns is the namespace the body was WRITTEN in \x2014; the callee's, not the call\n  site's. Threaded rather than read off the node because only a fn literal needs\n  it, and it needs it for the image registration (see the :fn arm)." (keyword #f "line") 137 (keyword #f "column") 1))))
